      "explanation": "Reflection across the \\(x\\)-axis keeps each point's \\(x\\)-coordinate and negates its \\(y\\)-coordinate. First write the original line as\n\\[y=\\frac{x+11}{3}.\\]\nNegating its output gives the reflected line\n\\[y=-\\frac{x+11}{3}=-\\frac13x-\\frac{11}{3}.\\]\nThus \\(m=-1/3\\) and \\(b=-11/3\\), so\n\\[m+b=-\\frac{12}{3}=\\boxed{-4}.\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
